# ---- The wrappers of a profile, generated by the build ----
#
#   wxl_add_ui_library(<profile> PROFILE <file.winxl-profile> [PARTS <n>])
#   wxl_generate_wrappers(<name> DIR <dir> PROFILE <file.winxl-profile> PARTS <n>
#                         [DOCS <language code>] [DECLARE_HEADERS]
#                         [OUT_PARTS <var>] [OUT_SURFACE <var>])
#
# wxl_add_ui_library makes the library of a profile, wxl.ui.<profile>
# (wxl::ui.<profile>), over wxl.ui.common, and the test of its declarative
# surface, wxl.ui.<profile>.surface-test. The library is the wrappers of the
# profile, generated by the build, and the hand-written sources of the profile
# layer, which wxl.ui.common hands over in its properties WXL_UI_PROFILE_SOURCES
# (absolute paths), WXL_UI_PROFILE_LIBRARIES and WXL_UI_PROFILE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES:
# a profile declared outside the tree goes through this function and builds
# the same sources the same way. <profile> is the stem of the profile file
# (full for full.winxl-profile), which is also the name of the directory of the
# wrappers. The library links wxl::ui.common PUBLIC. An application names it in
# wxl_add_executable(<target> UI wxl::ui.<profile> ...).
#
# The wrappers -- the classes, the enums and structs, the property tags, the
# schema -- are not in the repository: winui-srcgen writes them from the
# profile and the metadata of the restored packages, and wxl_add_ui_library
# makes that run a step of the build, so that a fresh clone needs nothing but
# the build itself and the build compiles exactly what the run wrote:
#
#   <build>/wxl.ui/<profile>/wxl/            the headers, <wxl/X.h> through the
#                                            directory above, a PUBLIC include
#                                            directory of the library; recorded
#                                            in the target property
#                                            WXL_WRAPPERS_DIR
#   <build>/wxl.ui/<profile>/wxl/parts/      wrapper-00.cpp ... wrapper-<n-1>.cpp,
#                                            sources of the library, and
#                                            schema_surface.cpp, the source of
#                                            wxl.ui.<profile>.surface-test
#
# In the build directory and not in the sources: what is generated belongs to
# the build that generated it -- its packages, its generator. The
# configurations of one build directory (Debug and Release of Ninja
# Multi-Config) share it: they generate the same files, and they run the
# generator under one name (the WXL_SHARED_FILE of winui-srcgen,
# wxl.gen/CMakeLists.txt), so a build of the other configuration runs it again
# only when that configuration's generator was linked anew. The steps are those
# of the target wxl.ui.<profile>.wrappers, which the library and its surface
# test depend on, so that every compile and every module scan of their sources
# -- which include the generated headers -- comes after them. wxl.ui.common
# does not depend on it and has no include path to the wrappers.
#
# The wrappers the library compiles are never documented: the /// comments
# would change no code, but a documented run rewrites every header -- and with
# them every source of the library and of its consumers would be compiled again
# -- whenever the language or the site is switched, and a reference file that
# does not read would stop the build of a library. The documentation site
# generates the same profile once more, documented, into a directory of its own
# (docs/CMakeLists.txt), with wxl_generate_wrappers, which does the generation
# for both.
#
# What the build can know before the run is what it declares. The parts have
# names fixed by PARTS (default 8: each takes about an eighth of the classes,
# where the controls alone, compiled as one source, are the longest compile of
# the tree), so they are the outputs of the run. The names of the headers come
# from the profile and the metadata, so with DECLARE_HEADERS -- for wrappers a
# build compiles -- they are taken from the output directory as the last run
# left it -- a glob, which the build checks again before it starts, and
# configures again when the set changed: after the first build, after a run
# that wrote a header more or less -- and declared as by-products of a second
# step after the run. Ninja then knows what writes them, and a source that
# includes a header the run rewrote is compiled again in the same build;
# undeclared, it would be compiled again only by the next one. A step of their
# own, which only touches its stamp: a header found by a new configure has no
# entry in Ninja's log yet, and as a by-product of the run itself it would have
# Ninja run the generator once more for nothing. This rests on an assumption to
# check on the Windows machine: the path a compile's dependency record names for
# a header is the node the by-product declares. An include spelled in another
# case, which Windows opens all the same, would be another node to Ninja, and a
# source including the header so would be compiled again only by the next build.
#
# Ninja's restat, which CMake sets on a custom command, keeps the rest as it
# is: the generator writes only the files that changed, so a run that changes
# nothing leaves the parts and the headers, and everything built from them,
# alone. generated.stamp, touched by the last command of the run, is the output
# it always writes.
#
# The command runs again when the generator, the list of the restore
# (wxl_restored_packages_file(), cmake/wxl_packages.cmake) or a file of the
# profiles changes: of the profile's own directory and of the tree's
# wxl.gen/profiles -- the profiles, types.json, fluent-symbols.json. Every one
# of them, and not only the profile and what it extends: profiles are JSON with
# comments, which CMake cannot read, so the chain of `extends` is not known
# here; and a profile outside the tree may extend one of the tree's.
#
# DOCS writes the metadata's documentation into the headers, in that language
# (winui-srcgen --docs --doc-language), and leaves doc_language.txt beside them.
#
# Refused at configure, each with its remedy: no target winui-srcgen (a
# directory configured without the root of the wxl tree, which builds the
# generator), no target wxl.ui.common, a profile file whose stem is not the
# name of the library, a directory src/wxl in wxl.ui (generated there by hand,
# it would shadow the generated headers on the include path src/), a profile
# that does not exist, PARTS outside 1 to 100 (the names of the parts have two
# digits).
# cmake/wxl_packages.cmake is included before.

include_guard(GLOBAL)

# Find PowerShell once, before any function uses it.
find_program(POWERSHELL_EXE NAMES pwsh powershell)
if(NOT POWERSHELL_EXE)
    message(FATAL_ERROR
        "No PowerShell found: wxl_add_ui_library needs it to read profile components. "
        "Install PowerShell (pwsh.exe or powershell.exe on PATH).")
endif()

function(wxl_generate_wrappers name)
    cmake_parse_arguments(PARSE_ARGV 1 A "DECLARE_HEADERS"
        "DIR;PROFILE;PARTS;DOCS;OUT_PARTS;OUT_SURFACE;COMPONENT_DIR;COMMON_DIR" "COMPONENTS;MANIFESTS")
    if(A_UNPARSED_ARGUMENTS OR A_KEYWORDS_MISSING_VALUES)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): unknown arguments '${A_UNPARSED_ARGUMENTS}' or "
            "keywords without a value '${A_KEYWORDS_MISSING_VALUES}'.")
    endif()
    if(NOT TARGET winui-srcgen)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): there is no target winui-srcgen, which generates "
            "the wrappers: ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR} is configured without the wxl tree that "
            "builds it. Configure the root of the wxl tree (tools\\build.ps1, or cmake --preset "
            "x64-dynamic there).")
    endif()
    if(NOT A_DIR)
        message(FATAL_ERROR "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): no DIR.")
    endif()
    if(NOT A_PROFILE)
        message(FATAL_ERROR "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): no PROFILE.")
    endif()
    cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH A_PROFILE NORMALIZE)
    if(NOT EXISTS "${A_PROFILE}" OR IS_DIRECTORY "${A_PROFILE}")
        message(FATAL_ERROR "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): no profile file ${A_PROFILE}.")
    endif()
    if(NOT A_PARTS MATCHES "^[0-9]+$" OR A_PARTS LESS 1 OR A_PARTS GREATER 100)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): PARTS ${A_PARTS}: the number of parts is from 1 to "
            "100.")
    endif()
    wxl_restored_packages_file(_wxl_packages)
    if(NOT _wxl_packages)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): no list of the restored packages; include "
            "cmake/wxl_packages.cmake before.")
    endif()
    get_target_property(_wxl_generator winui-srcgen WXL_SHARED_FILE)
    if(NOT _wxl_generator)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_generate_wrappers(${name}): winui-srcgen has no WXL_SHARED_FILE, the copy of "
            "it the steps run (wxl.gen/CMakeLists.txt).")
    endif()

    set(_wxl_out "${A_DIR}")
    cmake_path(GET A_PROFILE STEM LAST_ONLY _wxl_name)
    cmake_path(GET A_PROFILE PARENT_PATH _wxl_profiles_dir)
    cmake_path(GET CMAKE_CURRENT_FUNCTION_LIST_DIR PARENT_PATH _wxl_tree)

    math(EXPR _wxl_last "${A_PARTS} - 1")
    set(_wxl_parts "")
    foreach(_wxl_part RANGE ${_wxl_last})
        if(_wxl_part LESS 10)
            set(_wxl_part "0${_wxl_part}")
        endif()
        list(APPEND _wxl_parts "${_wxl_out}/parts/wrapper-${_wxl_part}.cpp")
    endforeach()
    set(_wxl_surface "${_wxl_out}/parts/schema_surface.cpp")
    set(_wxl_stamp "${_wxl_out}/generated.stamp")

    set(_wxl_profile_files "")
    foreach(_wxl_dir IN ITEMS "${_wxl_profiles_dir}" "${_wxl_tree}/wxl.gen/profiles")
        file(GLOB _wxl_found CONFIGURE_DEPENDS
            "${_wxl_dir}/*.winxl-profile"
            "${_wxl_dir}/types.json"
            "${_wxl_dir}/fluent-symbols.json")
        list(APPEND _wxl_profile_files ${_wxl_found})
    endforeach()
    list(REMOVE_DUPLICATES _wxl_profile_files)

    set(_wxl_docs "")
    if(DEFINED A_DOCS)
        set(_wxl_docs --docs --doc-language "${A_DOCS}")
    endif()

    set(_wxl_component_args "")
    if(A_COMPONENT_DIR)
        list(APPEND _wxl_component_args --component-dir "${A_COMPONENT_DIR}")
    endif()
    if(A_COMPONENTS)
        foreach(_wxl_comp IN LISTS A_COMPONENTS)
            list(APPEND _wxl_component_args --component "${_wxl_comp}")
        endforeach()
    endif()
    if(A_COMMON_DIR)
        list(APPEND _wxl_component_args --common-dir "${A_COMMON_DIR}")
    endif()

    add_custom_command(
        OUTPUT ${_wxl_parts} "${_wxl_surface}" "${_wxl_stamp}"
        COMMAND "${_wxl_generator}"
                --profile "${A_PROFILE}" --packages "${_wxl_packages}"
                --out "${_wxl_out}" --parts ${A_PARTS} ${_wxl_docs}
                ${_wxl_component_args}
        COMMAND "${CMAKE_COMMAND}" -E touch "${_wxl_stamp}"
        DEPENDS winui-srcgen "${A_PROFILE}" ${_wxl_profile_files} "${_wxl_packages}" ${A_MANIFESTS}
        WORKING_DIRECTORY "${_wxl_tree}"
        COMMENT "winui-srcgen: the wrappers of ${_wxl_name} -> ${_wxl_out}"
        VERBATIM)
    set(_wxl_steps "${_wxl_stamp}")
    if(A_DECLARE_HEADERS)
        file(GLOB _wxl_headers CONFIGURE_DEPENDS "${_wxl_out}/*.h")
        if(_wxl_headers)
            # The headers, by-products of a step after the run (see above).
            set(_wxl_headers_stamp "${_wxl_out}/headers.stamp")
            add_custom_command(
                OUTPUT "${_wxl_headers_stamp}"
                BYPRODUCTS ${_wxl_headers}
                COMMAND "${CMAKE_COMMAND}" -E touch "${_wxl_headers_stamp}"
                DEPENDS "${_wxl_stamp}"
                VERBATIM)
            list(APPEND _wxl_steps "${_wxl_headers_stamp}")
        endif()
    endif()
    add_custom_target(${name} DEPENDS ${_wxl_steps})

    if(A_OUT_PARTS)
        set(${A_OUT_PARTS} "${_wxl_parts}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    endif()
    if(A_OUT_SURFACE)
        set(${A_OUT_SURFACE} "${_wxl_surface}" PARENT_SCOPE)
    endif()
endfunction()

function(wxl_add_ui_library profile)
    cmake_parse_arguments(PARSE_ARGV 1 A "" "PROFILE;PARTS" "")
    if(A_UNPARSED_ARGUMENTS OR A_KEYWORDS_MISSING_VALUES)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_add_ui_library(${profile}): unknown arguments '${A_UNPARSED_ARGUMENTS}' or "
            "keywords without a value '${A_KEYWORDS_MISSING_VALUES}'.")
    endif()
    if(NOT TARGET wxl.ui.common)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_add_ui_library(${profile}): there is no target wxl.ui.common, the layer every "
            "profile stands on and the owner of the sources of the profile layer; add the "
            "directory wxl.ui before.")
    endif()
    if(NOT A_PROFILE)
        message(FATAL_ERROR "wxl_add_ui_library(${profile}): no PROFILE.")
    endif()
    cmake_path(ABSOLUTE_PATH A_PROFILE NORMALIZE)
    cmake_path(GET A_PROFILE STEM LAST_ONLY _wxl_name)
    if(NOT _wxl_name STREQUAL profile)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_add_ui_library(${profile}): the profile file ${A_PROFILE} is named "
            "${_wxl_name}; the library of a profile, and the directory of its wrappers, take "
            "the name of the profile file.")
    endif()
    get_target_property(_wxl_common_dir wxl.ui.common SOURCE_DIR)
    if(EXISTS "${_wxl_common_dir}/src/wxl")
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_add_ui_library(${profile}): ${_wxl_common_dir}/src/wxl exists: wrappers "
            "generated into the sources, which would be found on the include path "
            "${_wxl_common_dir}/src ahead of the ones this build generates. Delete the "
            "directory; the build generates the wrappers into ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/wxl.ui.")
    endif()
    if(NOT DEFINED A_PARTS)
        set(A_PARTS 8)
    endif()

    set(_wxl_target "wxl.ui.${profile}")
    set(_wxl_root "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/wxl.ui/${profile}")
    set(_wxl_out "${_wxl_root}/wxl")

    # Call the PowerShell script to read components from the profile chain.
    execute_process(
        COMMAND "${POWERSHELL_EXE}" -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File
                "${CMAKE_CURRENT_FUNCTION_LIST_DIR}/Read-ProfileComponents.ps1"
                -Profile "${A_PROFILE}"
                -ComponentDir "${_wxl_common_dir}/components"
        OUTPUT_VARIABLE _wxl_script_output
        RESULT_VARIABLE _wxl_script_result
        ERROR_VARIABLE _wxl_script_error
        OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
        ERROR_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
    )
    if(NOT _wxl_script_result EQUAL 0)
        message(FATAL_ERROR
            "wxl_add_ui_library(${profile}): PowerShell script Read-ProfileComponents.ps1 failed "
            "with exit code ${_wxl_script_result}:\n${_wxl_script_error}")
    endif()

    # Parse the script output: chain:<name>, component:<name>, dir:<path>, source:<file>, library:<target>.
    set(_wxl_chain_components "")
    set(_wxl_component_dirs "")
    set(_wxl_component_sources "")
    set(_wxl_component_libraries "")
    set(_wxl_manifests "")
    set(_wxl_current_component "")
    set(_wxl_current_dir "")

    string(REPLACE "\n" ";" _wxl_lines "${_wxl_script_output}")
    foreach(_wxl_line IN LISTS _wxl_lines)
        if(_wxl_line MATCHES "^(chain|component|dir|source|library):(.*)$")
            set(_wxl_type "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
            set(_wxl_value "${CMAKE_MATCH_2}")
            if(_wxl_type STREQUAL "chain")
                list(APPEND _wxl_chain_components "${_wxl_value}")
            elseif(_wxl_type STREQUAL "component")
                set(_wxl_current_component "${_wxl_value}")
            elseif(_wxl_type STREQUAL "dir")
                set(_wxl_current_dir "${_wxl_value}")
                list(APPEND _wxl_component_dirs "${_wxl_current_dir}")
                list(APPEND _wxl_manifests "${_wxl_current_dir}/component.json")
            elseif(_wxl_type STREQUAL "source")
                list(APPEND _wxl_component_sources "${_wxl_current_dir}/${_wxl_value}")
            elseif(_wxl_type STREQUAL "library")
                list(APPEND _wxl_component_libraries "${_wxl_value}")
            endif()
        endif()
    endforeach()

    # Add every manifest to CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS so CMake reconfigures when they change.
    foreach(_wxl_manifest IN LISTS _wxl_manifests)
        set_property(DIRECTORY APPEND PROPERTY CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS "${_wxl_manifest}")
    endforeach()

    # Chase the profile chain's extends and add each profile to CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS.
    set(_wxl_profile_chain "${A_PROFILE}")
    set(_wxl_visited_profiles "")
    while(_wxl_profile_chain)
        list(POP_FRONT _wxl_profile_chain _wxl_current_profile)
        if(_wxl_current_profile IN_LIST _wxl_visited_profiles)
            continue()
        endif()
        list(APPEND _wxl_visited_profiles "${_wxl_current_profile}")
        set_property(DIRECTORY APPEND PROPERTY CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS "${_wxl_current_profile}")

        # Read the profile to find its extends.
        file(READ "${_wxl_current_profile}" _wxl_profile_content)
        if(_wxl_profile_content MATCHES "\"extends\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\\[([^]]+)\\]")
            string(REGEX MATCHALL "\"([^\"]+)\"" _wxl_extends_matches "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
            cmake_path(GET _wxl_current_profile PARENT_PATH _wxl_profile_dir)
            foreach(_wxl_extend_match IN LISTS _wxl_extends_matches)
                if(_wxl_extend_match MATCHES "\"([^\"]+)\"")
                    set(_wxl_parent_name "${CMAKE_MATCH_1}")
                    set(_wxl_parent_profile "${_wxl_profile_dir}/${_wxl_parent_name}.winxl-profile")
                    list(APPEND _wxl_profile_chain "${_wxl_parent_profile}")
                endif()
            endforeach()
        endif()
    endwhile()

    wxl_generate_wrappers(${_wxl_target}.wrappers
        DIR "${_wxl_out}" PROFILE "${A_PROFILE}" PARTS "${A_PARTS}" DECLARE_HEADERS
        COMPONENT_DIR "${_wxl_common_dir}/components"
        COMPONENTS ${_wxl_chain_components}
        COMMON_DIR "${_wxl_common_dir}/src"
        MANIFESTS ${_wxl_manifests}
        OUT_PARTS _wxl_parts OUT_SURFACE _wxl_surface)

    get_target_property(_wxl_sources wxl.ui.common WXL_UI_PROFILE_SOURCES)
    get_target_property(_wxl_libraries wxl.ui.common WXL_UI_PROFILE_LIBRARIES)
    get_target_property(_wxl_includes wxl.ui.common WXL_UI_PROFILE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES)

    add_library(${_wxl_target} STATIC ${_wxl_sources} ${_wxl_component_sources} ${_wxl_parts})
    add_library(wxl::ui.${profile} ALIAS ${_wxl_target})
    add_dependencies(${_wxl_target} ${_wxl_target}.wrappers)
    target_compile_features(${_wxl_target} PUBLIC cxx_std_23)
    target_include_directories(${_wxl_target}
        PUBLIC "$<BUILD_INTERFACE:${_wxl_root}>"
               "$<BUILD_INTERFACE:${_wxl_component_dirs}>"
        PRIVATE ${_wxl_includes})
    # As in wxl.ui.common: nothing of the layer draws through GDI, and the few
    # files that paint a GDI surface lift it for themselves.
    target_compile_definitions(${_wxl_target} PRIVATE NOGDI)
    target_link_libraries(${_wxl_target}
        PUBLIC wxl::ui.common
        PRIVATE ${_wxl_libraries} ${_wxl_component_libraries})
    set_property(TARGET ${_wxl_target} PROPERTY WXL_WRAPPERS_DIR "${_wxl_out}")

    # The declarative surface, compiled the way an application sees it: linked
    # against the library only, so it inherits the PUBLIC include paths and not
    # the cppwinrt projection -- a winrt:: name leaking into a public header
    # breaks this target instead of quietly costing every consumer the
    # projection's parse time. With it, the generated schema's own test.
    add_library(${_wxl_target}.surface-test OBJECT
        "${_wxl_common_dir}/test/dsl_surface.cpp" "${_wxl_surface}")
    add_dependencies(${_wxl_target}.surface-test ${_wxl_target}.wrappers)
    target_link_libraries(${_wxl_target}.surface-test PRIVATE ${_wxl_target})

    # The bodies of the controls compiled as one source exceed the 65 279
    # sections of the default object format: MSVC stops with C1128 unless the
    # object is written as /bigobj. On every part, since which classes a part
    # holds, and how many, follows the profile and PARTS.
    set_property(SOURCE ${_wxl_parts} APPEND PROPERTY
        COMPILE_OPTIONS $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>:/bigobj>)

    # Last: this reads the targets' SOURCES to lay them out in the IDE.
    wxl_set_target_folders(${_wxl_target})
    wxl_set_target_folders(${_wxl_target}.surface-test PREFIX "tests")
endfunction()
